---
import ClubBase from '../../layouts/ClubBase.astro';
import race from '../../content/race.json';

// `/events/` — the races the club puts on, and the socials in between.
//
// ## What this page is, and the one thing it is not
//
// **A static list, and the links on it are pages rather than a database read.** There is one
// race and one social today, so a list painted from `store.socials` would be a round trip to
// learn something the build already knows — and a second social needs its own content page
// anyway, which is a deploy either way. When there are enough of these to be worth a query,
// this is the page that becomes one.
//
// The address is `/events/` because that is what the old Squarespace site published and Phase
// 5 keeps its paths. The schema calls a party a *social*, because the glossary reserves
// *event* for one running of one race in one year — see ADR-033. **Neither word is on the
// page**: a navigation label and a heading are written for whoever is reading them.
//
// ## ⚠️ The two data attributes are a contract with the Worker, not decoration
//
// `hideUnpublishedLinks()` in `worker/index.ts` regex-scans the served body for
// `data-social-link="<slug>"`, asks the database about each slug, and sets `hidden` on **the
// element it matched** for any it answers nothing for. So the attribute belongs on the `<li>`
// — the whole row, date tile included — and never on the `<a>` inside it, which would leave a
// dated row with its link removed.
//
// `[data-social-none]` ships `hidden` and is revealed only when *every* social link has been
// hidden. It lives inside the socials section because that is what it is about: the race
// above it is not a social and is never hidden.
//
// ## ⚠️ Nothing here states a fact it has not read
//
// The race's date, distance and headquarters come from `race.json`, which is where they live
// and which `/` already reads the same way. A copy in this markup would be a second place to
// change them, and the failure is silent — a page showing last year's date looks exactly like
// one showing this year's.
//
// ⚠️ **The party's date is not in this repository either, and it is still shown.** It is a
// `store.socials` column, and `renderSocialRow()` paints it onto the row from the record the
// Worker was already fetching to decide whether to show that row at all — so this costs no
// extra read and confirming a date stays an `update` and no deploy. Typing "12 December 2026"
// here would be the club announcing a date out of markup that nothing holds to the column it
// lives in, and the failure would be silent: a page showing last year's date looks exactly
// like one showing this year's.
//
// What ships is the "TBC" tile and "Details to be confirmed". That is what an unreachable
// database leaves in place, and it is the direction every other failure on this path takes.
//
// ## The surface
//
// `ClubBase`, not `Base` — ADR-048. This page is the club's own, and `club-pages.spec.ts` has
// said since that change that it *"becomes the races-and-events hub in the next change"*. The
// party's own page at `/events/<slug>/` takes money and keeps the old chrome until after the
// race on 1 November 2026; that fence is `club-chrome.spec.ts`'s and is untouched here.

// **Composed here rather than in the markup.** Prettier reflows adjacent expressions onto
// separate lines and Astro compresses the newline between them to nothing, which silently eats
// the space — this repository has already shipped "BristolBS3 1DB" and "live onour old site"
// that way. One expression cannot lose a join it does not have.
const raceDetails = `${race.date} · ${race.distance} · ${race.hqName}`;

// The tile's two halves, split from the one field that holds them. `dateShort` is "1 November";
// the month is cut to three letters because the tile is 4.25rem wide, which is a way of writing
// the month rather than a different fact.
const [raceDay = '', raceMonth = ''] = race.dateShort.split(' ');
---

<ClubBase
  title="Races and events — Southville Running Club"
  description="The races Southville Running Club organises, and the socials in between."
  canonical="https://new.southvillerunningclub.co.uk/events/"
>
  <header class="club-phead">
    <div class="club-wrap">
      <h1>Races and events</h1>
      <p class="club-lede">The races we organise and the socials in between.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="club-sec">
    <div class="club-wrap club-g2 club-split">
      <div>
        <p class="club-jump">
          Jump to: <a href="#races">Races</a>
          <a href="#socials">Social events</a>
        </p>

        <section id="races" aria-labelledby="races-heading">
          <h2 id="races-heading">Races</h2>
          <p>The races the club organises itself, and where to enter them.</p>

          <ul class="club-events">
            <li>
              {
                /* ⚠️ **Decorative, because the row already says the date in full.** Left
                  readable, a screen reader announces "1", "Nov" and then the whole date again
                  a line later. The fact is in the text beneath; this is a way of showing it. */
              }
              <p class="club-event-when" aria-hidden="true">
                <b>{raceDay}</b><span>{raceMonth.slice(0, 3)}</span>
              </p>
              <div>
                {
                  /* **`/nn/` and not `/nn/2026/`.** That address is evergreen — it paints on
                    whichever running is current from `entries.current_entry_state('nn')` — so
                    this link keeps working when 2027 is published, and the entry journey from
                    it is untouched by this change. */
                }
                <h3><a href="/nn/">Nightingale Nightmare</a></h3>
                <p class="club-small">{raceDetails}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="socials" aria-labelledby="socials-heading">
          <h2 id="socials-heading">Social events</h2>
          <p>Parties, and everything else the club does that is not a run.</p>

          <ul class="club-events">
            <li data-social-link="christmas-party-2026">
              {
                /* ⚠️ **Three elements that move together, and the shipped state is the
                  honest one.** "TBC" is what this tile says until the Worker has read a date
                  out of `store.socials`; `renderSocialRow()` then fills the two halves,
                  reveals them and hides this one. An unreachable database, or a date the
                  club has not confirmed, leaves exactly what is rendered here — which is why
                  the date is **not** written into this markup. It is a column, and confirming
                  one is an `update` and no deploy. */
              }
              <p class="club-event-when" aria-hidden="true">
                <b class="club-event-when-tbc" data-social-tbc>TBC</b><b
                  data-social-day
                  hidden></b><span data-social-month hidden></span>
              </p>
              <div>
                <h3>
                  <a href="/events/christmas-party-2026/">SRC Christmas Party 2026</a>
                </h3>
                <p class="club-small" data-social-details>Details to be confirmed</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>

          {
            /* Ships hidden and is revealed only when every social link above has been hidden.
              A list with no visible items and nothing beneath it reads as a broken page; this
              reads as true. */
          }
          <p data-social-none hidden>Nothing is coming up just now. Check back soon.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      {
        /* ⚠️ **A flat panel, `aria-hidden`, with nothing written on it** — `/about/`'s exactly,
          and for its reasons. A stripe pattern reads as a broken image and a bracketed caption
          is the placeholder this build may not publish. When the club supplies photographs,
          with consent from the people in them, this is replaced rather than filled in. */
      }
      <div class="club-photo club-photo-tall" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ClubBase>
